<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait import payments slip in September.</title>
<headline>Kuwait import payments slip in September.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payments made by Kuwaiti banks to finance imports fell to 116.0 million dinars in September from 119.4 million dinars in August, a Central Bank monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>The payments were 115.3 million dinars in September 1995.</p>
<p>			   Figures in millions of dinars</p>
<p>					Sept	  Aug	Sept '95</p>
<p>Documentary LCs		   81.4	  87.6	79.9</p>
<p>Bills for collection	    17.4	  16.3	18.1</p>
<p>Other payment orders	    17.2	  15.5	17.3</p>
<p>The relative importance of the U.S. dollar in the financing rose to 64.3 percent in September from 62.0 in August. That of the Japanese yen rose to 3.3 percent from 3.1 percent.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.2988 dinars)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom +965 243 1920</p>
